 "method": "For each building footprint (outer ring): roof = last returns (return number equal to the number of returns) of class 1 (unclassified) or 6 (building) inside the ring and more than 0.5 m from it, more than 2.0 m above the ground; ground = the median of class 2 (ground) points 1 to 8.0 m outside the ring (1 to 25.0 m when fewer than 3 are found). Height = 90th percentile of the roof elevations minus the ground; p50 = their median. No value unless there are at least 6 roof points and 3 ground points, at least 50 % of the last returns inside the inset ring are roof points, and the height is 2.0 to 250.0 m. Points read with PDAL readers.ept at resolution 2.0 m, one query per zoom-16 cell; every 2018 collection whose bounds meet the cell is pooled. Heights are differences within one point cloud, so its vertical datum cancels out.",
